requirements:
Mandates training and careful measurement to minimize errors, enforcing five specific precautions:
a) Calipers and other measuring instruments must be properly maintained and accurate;
b) Operators must precisely locate the correct point of measurement (PoM) on the tree;
c) The plane of the calipers must be kept at right angles (perpendicular) to the longitudinal axis of the tree;
d) Correct mechanical pressure must be applied at the moment of measurement; and
e) The caliper's bar must be pressed firmly against the tree bole to minimize sliding arm maladjustment errors.
